\ ==== help for words defined in loaded files ====

\ The ( a b -- c ) \ summary line above a definition in a loaded file becomes the
\ word's entry: man answers { :word :effect :summary }, help prints it, and
\ apropos matches the summary. Continuation lines starting with \ extend the
\ summary. A definition without the comment, or typed at the REPL, has no entry.

"( a b -- c ) \ the larger of two numbers, as a float
: larger 2dup < if nip else drop then ;

( xs -- total ) \ the sum of an array of floats,
\ folded left with +
: total 0 ' + reduce ;

: undocumented 1 ;

( -- ) \ a comment two lines up does not count

: separated 2 ;" "/tmp/docs-help.telic" write-file
"/tmp/docs-help.telic" load

\ -- man answers a frame built from the comment
' larger man frame>array . cr
' total man :summary @ . cr

\ -- help prints it like a reference entry
help larger
help total

\ -- apropos matches the summary of a loaded word and shows its effect
"folded left" apropos

\ -- no comment, or a blank line between comment and definition: no entry
' undocumented man . cr
' separated man . cr

\ -- a REPL definition has no entry, comment or not
( n -- n' ) \ typed here, not loaded
: at-repl 1+ ;
' at-repl man . cr

\ -- the words still run
3 7 larger . [ 1 2 3 ] total . 5 at-repl . cr
